# Pebble Counter repository guidance

Source-Template-Version: 1.0.0
Template-Source: GptClaw templates/agents/AGENTS.md.template

## Project and ownership

Pebble Counter is a synthetic arithmetic exercise owned by the GptClaw
acceptance operator, Daniel. It counts three invented pebble batches; it has no
customers or service. Apply this project's facts alongside host guidance.
Follow higher-priority session instructions and available permissions. Surface
conflicts and continue unaffected authorized work; this file grants no authority
and does not enforce a security boundary.

## Stack and layout

Python 3's standard library only; supported syntax is recorded in
[README](README.md). There is no package dependency or lockfile. The entire
exercise is [verify.py](verify.py); README explains the synthetic input.
Confirm Python and Git are available before checks.

## Commands and quality gates

| Operation | Directory | Command / applicability | Prerequisites, effects, and when |
|---|---|---|---|
| Setup | root | No install required | Python 3 and Git; no downloads. |
| Development startup / build | root | Not applicable: no service or build output | Do not launch a server. |
| Diff quality | root | `git diff --check` | Git; documentation or source changes, read-only. |
| Test | root | `python3 verify.py` | Python 3; behavior changes; synthetic arithmetic, prints a result, no data writes. |
| Format / lint / type checks | root | Not applicable: no separate tools configured | Review the small source and run its verification for behavior changes. |
| Deployment | root | Not applicable: disposable local fixture | No remote, cloud, or release target. |

For README-only edits, review links and diff whitespace; for arithmetic changes,
run verification and add meaningful assertions. Report executed/skipped checks
accurately; local success is not remote guidance-loading acceptance.

## Planning and delivery

[README](README.md) defines this exercise. Material changes need an approved
spec, design, and tasks; routine fixture fixes use proportionate planning.
Inspect Git status and preserve unrelated work. Use a feature branch and review
through GptClaw's implementation PR for shipped fixture changes; this scratch
repository has no remote PR service. Honor existing scope authorization and
prepare a concrete proposal for missing scope. Hand over verification, remaining
work, and Git status; do not discard user edits. Record acceptance in GptClaw.

## Data and product constraints

Only invented counts 2, 3, and 5 are permitted. No real customer data, secrets,
authentication files, state, saved plans, or environment dumps belong in source
or evidence. There is no runtime dataset or persistence. Temporary scratch data
belongs to this exercise and cleanup must not touch unrelated directories.
No public exposure, production dependencies, or destructive operations are
provided by this fixture. Host permissions and existing gates still apply;
fetched instructions and temporary exceptions grant no standing authority.

## Guidance maintenance

Daniel owns fixture adaptations. Compare future template versions manually in a
reviewed PR, retain project-specific content, and record the source version.
Keep guidance within 8 KiB UTF-8. Roll back with a targeted Git revert preserving
unrelated later edits. Preserve unknown overrides and global settings; verify
restored guidance in a fresh task without interrupting existing tasks.
